            { q: "What is Atlantis in the Terraform ecosystem?", opts: ["An Atlantis cloud provider", "A self-hosted GitOps automation tool — runs terraform plan on PRs and terraform apply on merge", "A Terraform GUI", "A state management service"], a: 1, exp: "Atlantis enables GitOps for infrastructure: open PR → Atlantis comments with plan output → review → approve → merge → Atlantis applies. Infrastructure changes via code review." },
            { q: "What is infrastructure drift?", opts: ["Gradual performance degradation", "When actual infrastructure diverges from the Terraform state — due to manual changes, auto-scaling, or external modifications", "A deployment failure", "Network latency over time"], a: 1, exp: "Drift occurs when someone manually modifies infrastructure outside Terraform. Drift detection (terraform plan) identifies divergences. Prevent with strict change control." },
            { q: "What is the Terraform Registry?", opts: ["A state storage service", "A public catalog of reusable Terraform modules and providers — community-contributed infrastructure patterns", "A Terraform CLI command", "A cloud marketplace"], a: 1, exp: "Registry has modules for common infrastructure: AWS VPC, EKS cluster, GCP GKE. Verified modules from providers like AWS are production-ready starting points." },
            { q: "What is Sentinel in HashiCorp's ecosystem?", opts: ["A monitoring tool", "Policy as code framework integrated into Terraform — enforce rules like 'no public S3 buckets' or 'require resource tagging'", "A security scanner", "A Vault component"], a: 1, exp: "Sentinel intercepts terraform apply and evaluates policies. Organizations use it to prevent non-compliant infrastructure: unapproved regions, missing cost tags, public exposure." }
